      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if there is a way to get a different union to show up in the Vec base class based on N without needing the subclass/cast stuff. Feels like we ought to be able to use template specialization based on N.\n\nDoes something like this work?\n\n\n  template \u003cint N, typename T\u003e VecStorage {};\n  template \u003ctypename T\u003e VecStorage\u003c1,T\u003e { union {...} };\n  template \u003ctypename T\u003e VecStorage\u003c2,T\u003e { union {...} };\n  template \u003ctypename T\u003e VecStorage\u003c4,T\u003e { union {...} };\n\n  template \u003cint N, typename T\u003e class Vec : public VecStorage\u003cN,T\u003e {\n     // voila, custom storage\n  };\n",
      "revId": "59e6fea9f08c1e478ac526365396b94c0f8f0d1d",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
